## 2. Graduated Runtime Manifold (GRM) Contract

The GRM is the only component allowed to touch hardware resources, scheduling, and memory.

### 2.1 Guarantees

| Guarantee                    | Description                                      |
|-----------------------------|--------------------------------------------------|
| Tick Determinism            | Same inputs + same seed → same entity states     |
| Soft Real-Time              | step() must complete within 1/tick_rate          |
| Memory Pressure Response    | When pressure ≥ threshold, triage is mandatory   |
| Epistemic Consistency       | Confidence values never increase without evidence|
| Void Safety                 | Reclaimed entities are unreachable after emit    |

### 2.2 Allowed Sacrifices (under pressure)

When `GRM.memory_pressure() ≥ 0.85` or frame budget is exceeded:

1. Lowest-utility agents may be liquidated (Cynical layer).
2. Render modes may be forced to Wireframe / GHOST.
3. Epistemic updates for non-visible entities may be deferred one tick.
4. Non-critical event emission may be coalesced.

The GRM never invents purpose, never increases confidence without evidence, and never resurrects a void-reclaimed entity without an explicit ontology-level rebirth relation.

### 2.3 Pressure API

```
GRM.memory_pressure() → Float ∈ [0.0, 1.0]
GRM.frame_budget_remaining() → Duration
GRM.request_liquidation(entity) → Bool   // only if caller has Agency
```

